#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""eesel — a simple CLI for the eesel.ai platform.

Auth model:
  * `eesel login`           opens dashboard.eesel.ai in your browser, the
                            page sends the workspace JWT back to a local
                            HTTP server we spin up briefly. Standard CLI
                            OAuth bridge pattern.
  * `eesel login --dev`     mints a local JWT against the dev secret and
                            auto-discovers workspace/agent IDs from your
                            local Postgres container (no browser needed).

Sessions: stored at ~/.config/eesel/sessions/<id>.json; each maps to one
ongoing chat with a stable taskId + message history. `current.json` tracks
which session is "active" so plain `eesel chat "msg"` knows where to send.

API surface used:
  POST /workspaces/token             (dashboard side, prod login bridge only)
  GET  /agents                       list agents in the workspace
  GET  /agents/{id}/triggers         list triggers configured for one agent
  POST /agents/sandbox/start         start/continue a chat, returns {taskId,streamUrl}
                                       optional triggerId → preview a scheduled
                                       trigger's context in chat
  GET  /agents/chat/{id}/raw-stream  SSE stream of UI message chunks
  POST /triggers/{id}/fire           manually enqueue a scheduled trigger
"""

